{
  "pr": {
    "title": "Avoid syntax errors for type variables with starred constraints (`UP040`, `UP046`, `UP047`, `RUF053`)",
    "body": "fixes #26954.\r\n\r\nAdds the missing tuple comma so starred contraints produce valid pep 695 fixes. Existing single element constraint tuples also keep their comma.\r\n\r\nTests cover aliases, classes and function type paramters across all four rules. All 2828 linter tests, clippy and hooks passed. checked the fixed code on python 3.12 and 3.14.",
    "commits": [
      "Preserve starred constraints in PEP 695 fixes (UP040, UP046, UP047, R…",
      "Mark starred constraint alias fixes unsafe outside stubs (UP040)",
      "Merge branch 'main' into fix/pep695-starred-constraints",
      "simplify display",
      "trim tests",
      "move new tests to end",
      "clippy"
    ]
  },
